vars:pre-request {
  baseUrl: http://localhost:3001
  pieceId: 3f0c7a52-8b1e-4d2a-9c3e-5a6b7c8d9e01
  otherPieceId: 5e2b9c14-7d3a-4f68-a1b0-c4d8e6f20a17
  secondPieceId: b0ed4901-0bb4-4592-93f4-7c6de1ce4890
  pictureId: 7a1d2e3f-4b5c-4d6e-8f70-81a2b3c4d5e6
  privatePictureId: c2d3e4f5-a6b7-4c8d-9e0f-1a2b3c4d5e6f
}

docs {
  Requests for the Ink API.

  1. Put your test user's email and password in the .env file in this folder (TEST_EMAIL, TEST_PASSWORD).
  2. Run "1 Sign in / Get a token".
  3. Run the "2 Pieces" folder top to bottom, then "3 Errors", then "4 Pictures".
  Writing goes through POST /api/pieces/{id}/sync with Yjs data (base64) that a script prepared, as if a device typed it.
  All the requests use the piece in pieceId (set above); change it to start clean.
  Privacy checks: "1 Sign in / Get a token (second user)" saves the second writer's token as secondToken. The "Privacy" requests in "5 Related" and the whole "6 Privacy" folder use it and must all be refused or empty.
  Tokens: token is the first writer, secondToken the second. Nothing needs signing in again in the middle of a run.

  Each request's Docs tab says what to expect.
}
